.TH PNM-DECODE 1 "November 2026" "PNM Viewer Toolkit" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pnm-decode \- decode a DOCSIS PNM capture to JSON
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pnm-decode
.RI [ OPTIONS ] " INPUT"
.SH DESCRIPTION
Read one local binary capture, identify its signature and version, and select
its parser automatically. No GUI or network connection is required.
By default, write formatted JSON beside INPUT with its extension replaced by .json.
Existing destinations, including symbolic links, are never replaced.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " PATH"
Choose the destination JSON file. Its parent directory must exist.
.TP
.B \-\-stdout
Write JSON to standard output instead of a file. Conflicts with --output.
.TP
.B \-\-header-only
Export common header metadata without measurement decoding or payload bytes.
.TP
.B \-\-rxmer-bit-loading
Export RxMER uniform-bit-loading analysis instead of raw capture JSON.
Default output is INPUT with .bit-loading.json extension. Conflicts with --header-only.
.TP
.B \-\-model NAME
Choose webui_mer_heuristic (default), ossi_candidate_defaults, or ideal_shannon.
.TP
.B \-\-start-hz HZ / \-\-stop-hz HZ
Provide both inclusive carrier-center bounds inside the capture, or omit both.
.TP
.B \-\-margin-db DB
Additional finite nonnegative MER margin; default 0.
.TP
.B \-\-max-bit-loading BITS
Known positive data-assignment cap: 2, 4, 6 through 14. Default 13 (8192-QAM).
This cap is an analysis choice, not inferred device capability.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show command help.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the executable version.
.TP
.B \-\-
End options; use before an input filename starting with a dash.
.SH FORMATS AND LIMITS
Supported measurement families include RxMER, channel estimate, constellation,
histogram, upstream pre-equalization and last update, FEC summary, spectrum,
modulation profiles, and latency. Enabled file-format version is 1.0.
Symbol capture supports header-only output; full decoding fails explicitly.
Latency is validated with synthetic inputs only.
Input and serialized JSON are limited to 16 MiB each (excluding the final output
newline). Decode budget is 65536 items. These are application policies.
.SH OUTPUT
JSON uses the core parser representation, including null for missing values
and iq pairs ordered as in-phase then quadrature. Diagnostics use standard error.
Modulation profiles include textual assignments, encoded assignment codes,
bit_loading and carrier_type (main_/skip_ fields for skip schemes).
Each profile includes bandwidth_bps beside profile_id and schemes, calculated
from data-carrier bit loading only. It is emitted for normal file output and
--stdout. The shared Rust helper also provides analysis with RF data-carrier
bandwidth in Hz and an
ideal gross theoretical_throughput_bps. The estimate excludes cyclic-prefix,
FEC and other PHY/MAC overhead; it is not measured application throughput.
Reserved or unknown assignments make the theoretical rate null.
The source documentation at docs/cli/usage.md links complete JSON examples for
each measurement family; latency and symbol-header examples are synthetic.
File output is published using a hard link from a complete temporary sibling.
Filesystems without hard-link support fail safely; use --stdout or another
filesystem. Normal failures clean up temporary files; forced termination may
leave a .pnm-decode-*.tmp file. No overwrite option is provided.
RxMER analysis uses original samples before display decimation. The weakest
measured carrier limits the uniform order. Missing readings retain nulls and
incomplete coverage. Gross rate assumes measured carriers are data and multiplies
their count by the uniform bits per symbol and subcarrier spacing. No LDPC/FEC,
cyclic-prefix, pilot/PLC or MAC overhead is subtracted. It is not measured payload
throughput or an error-free receiver guarantee. Model/margin/cap and scenario
statuses are included in the full-resolution analysis JSON.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, help, or version.
.TP
.B 1
File or stream I/O failure, including an existing destination.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command usage.
.TP
.B 3
Unknown or unsupported file identity, version, layout, or decoder.
.TP
.B 4
Malformed capture or resource/output limit exceeded.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
pnm-decode capture.bin
pnm-decode capture.bin --output results.json
pnm-decode capture.bin --stdout
pnm-decode capture.bin --header-only
pnm-decode rxmer.bin --rxmer-bit-loading --stdout
.fi
